# gradlew is a POSIX shell script - Docker builds run it inside a Linux
# container regardless of what platform checked the repo out. Windows'
# core.autocrlf converts it to CRLF on checkout otherwise, which breaks
# its shebang line inside the container ("./gradlew: not found" -
# discovered 2026-08-26 building the image locally on Windows for a
# manual deploy while GitHub Actions was down; Linux-hosted CI runners
# never hit this, since git there checks it out as LF either way, so
# this had been a real, latent Windows-only build break the whole time).
/gradlew text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
